# The fixed part of the package description: `make package-args` writes
# release/package.args from it and src/settings.def (a --setting line per row);
# `make test` fails when that file is out of date.
#
# Bridge 1.6 (NBT Manager with bridge 1.6), `status` (README, "Status": the
# menu label) and, optional, what NBT-AAD's iDrive plugin did
# (docs/upstream-interface.md, "Bridge 1.6"): `hold` (iDrive held on a blank
# state while Android Auto is on screen), `car-data` (the plugin's car data:
# src/protocol.hpp's kCds* names, in that order) and `net` (TCP 5277, the
# phone's Android Auto connection, on the CarPlay hotspot and the Wi-Fi Direct
# group). Not `show`: the manager would hand the application its surface,
# which the daemon does not use (it places its own), and stop it when nothing
# appeared there.
--app
android-auto
--compat
nbt_6.5_armv7
--bridge
1.6
--bridge-uses=
--bridge-optional
status,hold,car-data,net
--bridge-cds
driving.gear,sensors.PDCStatus,vehicle.dayNightChangeOver,driving.mode,driving.mode35up,driving.DSCActive,hmi.graphicalContext,communication.callStatus0,communication.callStatus1
--bridge-net
tcp:5277@uap0+wfd0
